  "caption": "Quinn joined a weightlifting club with Olympic dreams. The first snatch was wobbly, and the next day wrists, shoulder and low back were all grumbling.\n\nOlympic lifting isn't bad for your back by itself. Niggles in shoulders, wrists, low back, knees and elbows often come from limited mobility forcing shortcuts under speed and load.\n\nWhat can help: lift-specific mobility for the upper back, shoulders, hips and ankles, building strength to hold positions overhead rather than just reach them, coaching early, frequent moderate technique work instead of constant heavy singles, and scaling grip or stance while mobility improves.\n\nGet it checked for sudden severe pain, pain that travels down a limb, or overhead pain that won't settle.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
